The MIT License above covers the original code of this project. The following
third-party material is used and is not covered by the copyright line above.

1. NASA/JPL Horizons data

   The orbital positions of Chiron (2060), Ceres (1), Pallas (2), Juno (3) and
   Vesta (4) in js/ephemeris.js were generated with tools/build_ephemeris.py
   from data provided by the Solar System Dynamics group of the Jet Propulsion
   Laboratory (JPL), California Institute of Technology, for NASA:

       JPL Horizons On-Line Ephemeris System
       https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/horizons/

   Data produced by NASA/JPL is used here with acknowledgement of the source.
   NASA and JPL do not endorse or sponsor this project, and their names must
   not be used to suggest that they do. The data is provided without warranty;
   the values in js/ephemeris.js are resampled and rounded versions of the
   Horizons output.

